From: 24bit192kHz <118996408+24bit192kHz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] [local] dgpu: abort runtime power-on without power good

DGON stops waiting for DGFX_PWRGD after 100 ms but currently releases the
GPU reset and enables its PCIe link even when the rail never becomes ready.
The bootblock already leaves the GPU off on the same timeout.

Recheck power good after the bounded wait. If it is still low, disable the
link, assert reset, turn off the power request and allow the same 100 ms
off settling time as DGOF before returning. Do not release reset or enter
the link-up wait on this path. A signal that becomes ready at the final
recheck may proceed normally. Successful and already-powered paths stay
unchanged for stable power good. DGLW's independent link-timeout policy is
outside this patch.

Source-only proposal, not installed firmware. Baseline inspected:
coreboot c57exp 84126e3fc1e4129f5be9af44d633736cea68d169;
acpi/dgpu.asl SHA-256
1cd672880aca951c7801e4d7076472fc96e76fbb7ce7d72f8af1c27094201afa.
The file is also reconstructed exactly from local patch 0012; subsequent
patches 0013..0028 do not change it. Apply after 0028 with git am (or
patch -p1). Revert its resulting commit, or reverse the source change with
patch -R -p1 before rebuilding, to revert the source.
No ROM, CMOS, EC or target settings are changed by adding this patch.

Offline validation is in tools/re-audit/tests/test_dgpu_power_policy.py:
it checks exact forward/reverse application and executes the patched AML
methods in ACPICA with fake GPIO helpers and a simulated link. This tests
control flow, not electrical behavior, ACPI OS recovery, or successful sleep.
DGON remains a void method; PGPU _STA observes the cleared power-request
latch through DGST. Hardware validation requires separate user approval.

Validated on 2026-10-09 with iasl/acpiexec 20251212: 10 tests passed,
including compilation of both the complete baseline and patched existing
T480 build/dsdt.asl (baseline SHA-256
a3ba8b977b03fcfe5b2b6c189bba73db66b8f0d56eb82c990ee48d00ebcd3b26).
Both DSDTs compiled with 0 errors, 0 warnings and the same 29 remarks.
Fixture GPIO identifiers are anchored in the T480 variant/dgpu.h and the
selected gpio_soc_defs.h: GPP_E22=118, GPP_E23=119 and GPP_F3=123;
the actual preprocessed DSDT and matching headers are checked together.
Run with T480_COREBOOT_ROOT pointing to this matching source/build tree:
python3 -m unittest discover -s tools/re-audit/tests \
    -p test_dgpu_power_policy.py -v

---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/sklkbl_thinkpad/acpi/dgpu.asl | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/sklkbl_thinkpad/acpi/dgpu.asl b/src/mainboard/lenovo/sklkbl_thinkpad/acpi/dgpu.asl
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/sklkbl_thinkpad/acpi/dgpu.asl
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/sklkbl_thinkpad/acpi/dgpu.asl
@@ -47,6 +47,15 @@ Scope (\_SB.PCI0.RP01)
 			Sleep (1)
 			Local0++
 		}
+		/* A failed rail must not release reset or enable the PCIe link. */
+		If (!\_SB.PCI0.GRXS (GPIO_DGFX_PWRGD)) {
+			LNKD = 1
+			\_SB.PCI0.CTXS (GPIO_GPU_RST)
+			\_SB.PCI0.CTXS (GPIO_1R8VIDEO_AON_ON)
+			Sleep (100)
+			Return
+		}
+
 		Sleep (10)
 
 		\_SB.PCI0.STXS (GPIO_GPU_RST)
